<article class="env-corollary" id="032E">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/032E">Corollary <span data-tag="032E">3.4.1.6</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a commutative diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation" id="032F">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="032F" href="/tag/032F">3.41</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation} \label{diagram:homotopy-pullback-square55} \begin{gathered} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ X_{01} \ar [r] \ar [d]^{q'} &amp;  X_0 \ar [d]^{q} \\ X_1 \ar [r] &amp;  X, } \end{gathered}\end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> where $X$ is a Kan complex. Then (<a data-tag="032F" href="/tag/032F">3.41</a>) is a homotopy pullback square if and only if the induced map </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \theta : X_{01} \rightarrow X_0 \times _{X} X_1 \hookrightarrow X_{0} \times _{X}^{\mathrm{h}} X_{1} \]
</div>
<p> is a weak homotopy equivalence. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Proposition <a data-tag="00UV" href="/tag/00UV">3.1.8.1</a>, we can factor $q$ as a composition $X_0 \xrightarrow {w} X'_0 \xrightarrow {q'} X$, where $w$ is a weak homotopy equivalence and $q'$ is Kan fibration. We then have a commutative diagram 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ X_{01} \ar [r]^-{\theta } \ar [d]^{\rho } &amp;  X_{0} \times _{X}^{\mathrm{h}} X_{1} \ar [d] \\ X'_{0} \times _{X} X_{1} \ar [r] &amp;  X'_{0} \times _{X}^{\mathrm{h}} X_{1}, } \]
</div>
<p>
       where the bottom horizontal map is a weak homotopy equivalence (Proposition <a data-tag="0329" href="/tag/0329">3.4.0.7</a>) and the right vertical map is also a weak homotopy equivalence (Proposition <a data-tag="032B" href="/tag/032B">3.4.0.9</a>). It follows that $\theta $ is a weak homotopy equivalence if and only if $\rho $ is a weak homotopy equivalence. By virtue of Proposition <a data-tag="010N" href="/tag/010N">3.4.1.2</a>, this is equivalent to the requirement that the diagram (<a data-tag="032F" href="/tag/032F">3.41</a>) is a homotopy pullback square. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
